      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;formatting&#34;&gt;Formatting&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;wav&#34;&gt;.wav&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;.wav&lt;/code&gt; is a container format based on Microsoft/IBM’s Resource Interchange File Format (RIFF). It is primarily used to store uncompressed Pulse-Code Modulation (PCM) audios, offering the highest audio quality at the cost of large file sizes. Structurally, a &lt;code&gt;.wav&lt;/code&gt; file is organized as a sequence of chunks. Each chunk consists of a header identifying its type, a field specifying the size of its contents, and the corresponding data payload.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
